From d51df17505f4f03e624522ef9e4b2eebafe1d5b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:42:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: name the incoming ref in full when the
 protected-win preflight refuses

The blocker line truncated the ref to 12 characters, so a live run against upstream/master printed
"upstream/mas" - a string that resolves to nothing if the operator pastes it back. It now prints
the ref as given plus the sha it resolved to, which is what the resolution record has to key on.

Found by running the guard against a real upstream ref rather than only its fixtures. That run is
banked as the RED half of its two-halves evidence:
research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/rank3-r10/73-protected-win-preflight-LIVE-upstream.txt
- 6 of the 7 registered wins collide with upstream/master today and every one is REFUSED.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Lane: lane-209
Measured-effect: none - one diagnostic message string; 14/14 tests still green.
---
 tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py b/tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py
index 6bec53b8e6..86fba9a0b7 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py
@@ -1332,7 +1332,8 @@ def cmd_protected_win_check(repo: str, cfg: dict, args) -> int:
             match = r
             break
         if match is None:
-            unresolved.append((c, ["no resolution recorded for (%s, %s)" % (wid, incoming[:12])]))
+            unresolved.append((c, ["no resolution recorded for (%s, %s @ %s)"
+                                   % (wid, incoming, inc_full[:9])]))
             continue
         bad = _resolution_problems(match)
         bad += ["evidence locator %r does not resolve" % e
